  "id": "task-complexity",
  "term": "task complexity",
  "definition": "Task complexity is the degree of cognitive demand built into a task, based on how its design or conditions require attention and mental resources during performance. In this context, tasks can vary in complexity level, which can influence both how efficiently a person works and the quality of the final outcome.",
